I should involve the security agent if changes touch authentication, networking, parsing, file I/O, or shell execution. The test file seems to involve file I/O, but the change is more about reading files in docs and tests. I’m thinking it might be safer to dispatch the security agent anyway, though it could be overdoing it. Since closures and docs might affect file I/O, maybe I can have the reviewer and security agent work in parallel. I’ll need to list available agents, like "reviewer," "security," and "tester," and see if I should use bash for that too."}]}

